        "en": "Manglerud Church"
      },
      "summary": {
        "nb": "Manglerud kirke er soknekirke for Manglerud menighet i Søndre Aker prosti i Oslo bispedømme i Bydel Østensjø i Oslo kommune. Den er bygget som en langkirke i 1963 og ligger i drabantbyen Manglerud i Oslo kommune.\nArkitekt for kirken var Carl Corwin. Byggverket er i betong og har 310 sitteplasser.",
        "en": "Manglerud Church is a church in Oslo, Norway. The church was consecrated in December 1963. It is a parish church for Manglerud congregation. 400 seats, in addition to an adjacent church hall with 200 seats, as well as a smaller hall with 50 seats. There are also a small chapel, a baptismal sacristy and a youth activity room attached to the building. Manglerud Church is located above and on the south side of the E 6 highway and the subway at Ryen Station. It is easily visible with its high, steep ceilings and a slender, separate bell tower."
      },
